{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_4>\nimport sys\nfrom math import factorial\n\ndef A(n, k):\n    return factorial(n) // factorial(n - k)\n\ndef solve():\n    n, mod = map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split())\n    \n    if n == 1:\n        print(0)\n        return\n    \n    z = [1]\n    total = 0\n    \n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        new_z = [0] * (i * i // 2)\n        \n        for j, val in enumerate(z):\n            if val:\n                for k in range(i):\n                    new_z[i - k - 1 + j] += val\n        \n        d = [0] * (len(z) + 1)\n        for w in range(len(z) - 1, -1, -1):\n            d[w] = (d[w + 1] + z[w]) % mod\n        \n        e = [0] * (len(d) + 1)\n        f = [0] * (len(d) + 1)\n        for w in range(len(d)):\n            e[w + 1] = (e[w] + d[w]) % mod\n            f[w + 1] = (f[w] - w * d[w]) % mod\n        \n        current_contribution = 0\n        for jj in range(len(z)):\n            L = jj + 2\n            R = min(len(z) - 1, i + jj)\n            if R >= L:\n                diff_e = (e[R + 1] - e[L]) % mod\n                diff_f = (f[R + 1] - f[L]) % mod\n                term = (diff_e * (i + 1 + jj) + diff_f) % mod\n                current_contribution = (current_contribution + term * z[jj]) % mod\n        \n        total = (total + current_contribution * A(n, n - i)) % mod\n        z = new_z\n    \n    print(total % mod)\n\nsolve()\n</your_rewritten_code_4>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        new Main().solve();\n    }\n\n    private long factorial(int n) {\n        long result = 1;\n        for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++) {\n            result = (result * i) % MOD;\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    private long modPow(long base, long exp, long mod) {\n        long result = 1;\n        base = base % mod;\n        while (exp > 0) {\n            if ((exp & 1) == 1) {\n                result = (result * base) % mod;\n            }\n            base = (base * base) % mod;\n            exp >>= 1;\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    private long modInverse(long a, long mod) {\n        return modPow(a, mod - 2, mod);\n    }\n\n    private long A(int n, int k) {\n        long result = 1;\n        for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n            result = (result * (n - i)) % MOD;\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    private static final long MOD = 1_000_000_007;\n\n    public void solve() {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        int mod = sc.nextInt();\n\n        if (n == 1) {\n            System.out.println(0);\n            return;\n        }\n\n        List<Long> z = new ArrayList<>();\n        z.add(1L);\n\n        long total = 0;\n\n        for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++) {\n            int newZSize = i * i / 2;\n            List<Long> newZ = new ArrayList<>(Collections.nCopies(newZSize, 0L));\n\n            for (int j = 0; j < z.size(); j++) {\n                long val = z.get(j);\n                if (val != 0) {\n                    for (int k = 0; k < i; k++) {\n                        int idx = i - k - 1 + j;\n                        if (idx < newZSize) {\n                            newZ.set(idx, (newZ.get(idx) + val) % mod);\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n\n            List<Long> d = new ArrayList<>(Collections.nCopies(z.size() + 1, 0L));\n            for (int w = z.size() - 1; w >= 0; w--) {\n                d.set(w, (d.get(w + 1) + z.get(w)) % mod);\n            }\n\n            List<Long> e = new ArrayList<>(Collections.nCopies(d.size() + 1, 0L));\n            List<Long> f = new ArrayList<>(Collections.nCopies(d.size() + 1, 0L));\n            for (int w = 0; w < d.size(); w++) {\n                e.set(w + 1, (e.get(w) + d.get(w)) % mod);\n                long temp = (f.get(w) - (long)w * d.get(w)) % mod;\n                if (temp < 0) temp += mod;\n                f.set(w + 1, temp);\n            }\n\n            long currentContribution = 0;\n            for (int jj = 0; jj < z.size(); jj++) {\n                int L = jj + 2;\n                int R = Math.min(z.size() - 1, i + jj);\n                if (R >= L) {\n                    long diffE = (e.get(R + 1) - e.get(L)) % mod;\n                    if (diffE < 0) diffE += mod;\n                    long diffF = (f.get(R + 1) - f.get(L)) % mod;\n                    if (diffF < 0) diffF += mod;\n                    long term = (diffE * (i + 1 + jj) + diffF) % mod;\n                    currentContribution = (currentContribution + term * z.get(jj)) % mod;\n                }\n            }\n\n            total = (total + currentContribution * A(n, n - i)) % mod;\n            z = newZ;\n        }\n\n        System.out.println((total % mod + mod) % mod);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.85\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-8.689979586051777e-05, -